## 🚀 **Quick Start**

### Prerequisites
- Go 1.21+
- Redis 7+
- libpcap (for packet capture)
- Docker (optional)

### Installation

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/yourorg/fraud-detection.git
cd fraud-detection

# Install dependencies
go mod download

# Build
make build

# Run with Docker
docker-compose up -d
```

### Configuration

```yaml
# config.yaml
detection:
  # TCP fingerprint comparison tolerances
  tcp:
    mss_tolerance: 8       # ±8 bytes for VPN/MTU changes
    ws_tolerance: 1        # ±1 step for proxy normalization  
    ttl_tolerance: 1       # ±1 hop for route changes
    sack_required: true    # SACK must match exactly
    ts_required: true      # Timestamp must match exactly
  
  # Risk thresholds
  risk:
    allow_threshold: 30    # 0-29 = allow
    challenge_threshold: 60 # 30-59 = challenge, 60+ = block
  
  # Cloud provider detection
  cloud:
    refresh_interval: 3600 # Update AWS/GCP ranges every hour
    enabled: true
  
  # Redis
  redis:
    addr: localhost:6379
    password: ""
    db: 0
    fingerprint_ttl: 25    # TTL for SYN fingerprints (seconds)
    session_ttl: 1800      # Session TTL (30 minutes)

# Packet capture
pcap:
  interface: eth0          # Network interface to capture
  buffer_size: 1600        # Capture buffer size
  bpf_filter: "tcp[tcpflags] & tcp-syn != 0"  # BPF filter
```

